* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedUniversalCachedPipeline`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedNodeTopologyCompletion`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedRule4bReferenceAgreement`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedExtendedNodeSemanticCompletion`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedOriginalSpatialObservableCompletion`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedCumulativeChildShapeRecovery`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedRankedChildPermutation`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedRankedProjectionTransport`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedUniversalDescriptorCompleteness`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedUniversalSemanticComposition`
* `TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedCumulativeAssemblyRecovery`

Every public `def`, `abbrev`, `theorem` and `structure` is listed, together with the nine default
constructors of the authored structures
(`LocalizedRerootCompoundRule4bcComparisonObservable.mk`,
`LocalizedDescriptorBearingRule3NodeWithCompletionObligations.mk`,
`LocalizedRule3CyclicEndpointCompletion.mk`, `LocalizedRule3CyclicEndpointCanonicalEvidence.mk`,
`LocalizedOriginalNodeObservableCompletionObligations.mk`, `RuntimeCache.mk`,
`LocalizedOriginalSpatialObservableFields.mk`, `LocalizedOriginalEntryAxisRoutingFields.mk`,
`LocalizedKeyLayersNonempty.mk`).  Auto-generated structure projections, auto-generated recursors
and derived instances are not separate authored declarations and are not asserted.  Source
`private` helpers are proof-internal and are likewise not listed.  There are 348 public authored
declarations and 9 authored constructors, for 357 distinct `assert_kernel_only` commands in total.

The batch is proof-closed at kernel authority, but it is **not** a claim of completed universal
chemistry.  In particular, the capstone `LocalizedUniversalSemanticComposition` retains exactly one
explicit Rule-45 comparison-agreement premise (`LocalizedRerootCompoundRule45ComparisonAgreement`)
on each of its two `referenceState` transport theorems.  The certificate checks the kernel closure
of those stated theorems; it does not discharge, remove or assume away that premise.  The two
under-construction workstreams `A` and `B` are not imported here.

This file contains only import and `assert_kernel_only` commands.  It defines no proofs, performs no
evaluation, and adds no trust bypass.  Prior kernel certificates and runtime probes are NOT imported
and their checks are NOT rerun here.
-/

